  "answer": "The goal was not met: only 3 of the 5 challenging settings were confirmed, and all three are at the recorded timing (0 s shift) with the cars sped up. They are 023b7fcc at 1.25x speed, 09a95ffa at 1.5x and 096988dd at 2x. Every repeat at each of these settings failed. Each still has only a few runs, so its 90% range only just clears one half. In the first two, the policy itself was at fault: it drifted left out of its lane, even at 2 Hz planning. In 023b7fcc it hit a car driving alongside, and in 09a95ffa it closed on a slow car ahead without braking. The 096988dd case is weak evidence. Car 9 already overlaps the ego at handoff and looks like a smeared ghost on camera, which points to a bad replayed track rather than the policy, even though no run was flagged as a possible artifact. The other six scenes never failed at any setting tried. Most of those settings had one or two runs, so this is a hint that they are safe, not a measured rate.",
